# Dukascopy tick datasets — bulk binary, and the gold Parquet exceeds GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file limit. The pipeline in <symbol>_tick_data/dukascopy/code/
# rebuilds all of it from Dukascopy in ~15 minutes, and logs/manifest_by_hour.csv
# carries a SHA256 for every raw file, so the artefacts are reproducible rather
# than stored. Patterns are wildcarded by symbol: the gold-only versions let a
# partial silver download get swept in by a broad `git add`.
research/*_tick_data/dukascopy/raw/
research/*_tick_data/dukascopy/processed/*.parquet
research/*_tick_data/dukascopy/processed/*.csv.gz
research/*_tick_data/dukascopy/processed/parts/
research/*_tick_data/dukascopy/processed/parts*/

# 10AM study: regenerable intermediates (session_ticks is 1.25 GB)
research/gold_10am_flip/data/*.npy
research/gold_10am_flip/data/*.pkl

# Micro-Q3 audit: derived NY/Melbourne tick arrays and 1-minute bars, rebuilt by
# research/microq3/code/build_ny.py from the master parquet in ~3 minutes.
research/microq3/data/
research/microq3/data_holdout/
research/gold_holdout_tick_data/

# Derived tick-aligned label arrays for the goldmap phase, rebuilt in seconds by
# research/goldmap/code/tenam_holdout.py from the NY arrays. Hundreds of MB each.
research/goldmap/results/*.npy
research/goldmap/data/

# in-sample tick-path cache: a regenerable 1.3 GB artifact, never a repo file
research/insample/results/*.npz
